#N canvas 40 60 1280 940 12;
#X declare -path ..;
#X obj 0 0 cnv 1 1280 46 empty empty 02\ \ \ Activation\ functions\ \ =\ \ waveshapers 14 23 0 20 #1d3557 #ffffff 0;
#X obj 1110 910 declare -path ..;
#X text 800 910 finds the nn.* objects one folder up ->, f 42;
#X text 20 910 neuralplay - Moisés Horta Valenzuela / SEMILLA.AI Studio, f 70;
#X text 20 56 The weighted sum of a neuron can be any number. The ACTIVATION FUNCTION decides what the neuron passes on. To a musician it is a transfer curve - a waveshaper \, a distortion. Push a sine wave through it and listen., f 175;
#X obj 10 96 cnv 1 390 600 empty empty THE\ IDEA 8 12 0 13 #eef1f5 #1d3557 0;
#X text 20 122 Without a non-linear curve \, any network - however deep - collapses into one big linear mixer: nothing new can emerge. All the interesting behaviour of neural networks comes from these curves., f 52;
#X text 20 203 DRIVE is how hard you push the signal into the curve (the weights do that inside a neuron). OFFSET is the bias: it moves the signal to a different part of the curve. The orange bar under the plot shows the range of the curve you are using., f 52;
#X text 20 299 HISTORY: step (1943 \, 1958) - sigmoid and tanh (1986) made learning with gradients possible \, but their flat ends kill the gradient in deep nets - ReLU (2010) fixed that and started deep learning - GELU and swish (2016-17) live inside transformers - sin (SIREN \, 2020) for nets that represent signals., f 52;
#X text 20 410 SYMMETRY = HARMONICS. Odd curves \, f(-x) = -f(x) (tanh \, sin \, sign \, softsign \, hardclip) \, add only odd harmonics. Asymmetric curves (sigmoid \, relu \, elu \, gelu \, swish) add even harmonics and a DC offset ([hip~ 5] removes it). An even curve \, f(-x) = f(x) (gauss) \, sounds an octave up: both halves of the wave are folded the same way., f 52;
#X obj 410 96 cnv 1 430 600 empty empty PLAY:\ push\ a\ sine\ through\ the\ curve 8 12 0 13 #e3f0fb #1d3557 0;
#X obj 430 140 hsl 150 15 55 880 1 1 empty l02-freq frequency\ (Hz) 0 -8 0 11 #fcfcfc #000000 #000000 3700 1;
#X floatatom 588 139 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X obj 430 180 hsl 150 15 0 8 0 1 \$0-drive l02-drive drive 0 -8 0 11 #fcfcfc #000000 #000000 1900 1;
#X floatatom 588 179 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X obj 430 220 hsl 150 15 -2 2 0 1 \$0-offset l02-offset offset\ (bias) 0 -8 0 11 #fcfcfc #000000 #000000 7400 1;
#X floatatom 588 219 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
